                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a great game with lot's of character and full of references to anime, movies etc. Clearly made with lot's and lot's of love. Incremental ethusiasts will enjoy this quite a bit. The gameplay loop reminds me of reincarnation mangas with the crafting mechanic and such which i like a lot.\r\n\r\nIt could however use some small quality of life changes to make it really shine like descriptions and UI changes. For example if you go into the crafting menu and choose a target you want to craft items for, the game gives you 2 item options to choose from but if you don't want to craft either you can't just back out of the menu, you need to change to another tab and then back to the crafting one. Crafting menu also does not show what items the units currently have so to check that you have to go back to the Unit tab and then back to the Crafting tab.\r\n\r\nAnother example are the items in dungeons. You cannot inspect the stats of an item without picking it up first which means that if you have an item that gives let's say +30 max health and you pick up an item that does not have that, then pick up your original item back up, you will lose those extra health points. Meaning if you had 130/130 health before switching items, you will now have 100/130 health. \r\n\r\nFixing small things like these would make the already fun game infinitely better.",
